name: sim.getObjects
description: Retrieves object handles. Use this in a loop where index starts at 0 and is incremented to get all object handles in the scene
luaSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.getObjects(int index, int objectType)
pythonSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.getObjects(int index, int objectType)
inputs:
1. index: object index. First object is located at index 0
2. objectType: object type (sim.sceneobject_shape, sim.sceneobject_joint, etc. (see the object types) or sim.handle_all for any type of object
outputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the object or -1 if no object is located at that index
